117.m:
Having offered barley saying 'You are barley', [he offers] sesame seeds everywhere for the ancestors: / 'You are sesame, sacred to Soma, created by the gods as a cow-sacrifice;
united by the ancients with water, gratify with the funeral oblation our ancestors [and] the worlds, svadhā!'—thus.
[Saying] 'śrīś ca te', he should offer a flower in a golden or silver vessel,

